a071:
I changed `packages/components/src/components/text/Text.tsx` so that a disabled `as="link"` text is inert. I did not run builds or tests, did not install anything, and did not commit.

The fix is in `wrapIfAsLink`. When `disabled` is true, the inner anchor:
- drops `href`, so it cannot navigate on click, Enter or middle click and is not focusable;
- gets `tabindex="-1"`, which also overrides any consumer-supplied tabindex;
- gets `aria-disabled="true"`;
- gets the `is-disabled` class, which the existing theme rule `a.is-disabled` already styles.

When `disabled` is false, `href`, `tabindex` and `aria-disabled` pass through or stay unset, so non-disabled links render as before.

Not covered: with `as="link"` and `ellipsis="start"` and no `ellipsisOffset`, the component renders a root `<a>` with no `href` and no `attrs`. That path already has no navigation, so I left it alone. Say if you want it handled too.

